J.2 Complexity Computation

The complexity vector is

C(\mathcal A) = (C_{\mathrm{state}}, C_{\mathrm{model}}, C_{\mathrm{compute}}, C_{\mathrm{intervention}}, C_{\mathrm{validation}}).

For the linear benchmark:

· C_{\mathrm{state}}: number of state variables retained (1 for \mathcal A_1, 2 for \mathcal A_2, 1 for \mathcal A_3).
· C_{\mathrm{model}}: number of parameters (2 for \mathcal A_1, 4 for \mathcal A_2, 2 for \mathcal A_3).
· C_{\mathrm{compute}}: floating-point operations per simulation step.
· C_{\mathrm{intervention}}: cost of applying an intervention in the abstract model vs. the reference.
· C_{\mathrm{validation}}: number of samples required to establish validity at the desired confidence.

